WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:01.234
[suspenseful music]

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:01.868
[knock at door]

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:03.636
Hi, Cesar!

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:04.804
Hi, guys.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:05.572
How are you?

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:06.706
Good morning!

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.375
I have a surprise for
your final challenge.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.710
NARRATOR: For the past month,
Cesar has worked closely

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:13.446
with the Calderones, a
family of first responders

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:16.182
with a red-zone pit
bull named Bella.

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:17.117
After two attacks--

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:17.917
Bella!

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:18.785
Bella!

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.320
[aggressive barking]

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:22.122
NARRATOR: --the family may
need to surrender Bella if they

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.290
can't control her excitement.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.493
CESAR: The last time I came
here to work with Bella

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.928
it was because she escaped
out of the front door

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:30.497
to attack another dog.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:33.633
I need to know that we worked
through her dog aggression.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.336
To put Bella and
Jennifer to a final test,

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:39.939
I'm going to have my son Andre
walk a dog by the front door

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:41.975
to see if Jennifer
can keep Bella

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:43.676
in a calm surrender state.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:44.644
All right, Andre.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.420
[bella growling]

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:54.654
Tsch!

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:55.889
Tsch!

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:58.425
I could see Bella
switching into attack mode.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:00.160
Her body was getting tense.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.362
Her eyes were getting
fixated on the husky.

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:05.231
I just need to do a proper
correction to remind Jennifer

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:06.800
how to keep Bella calm.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.768
Tsch!

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.170
There you go.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.871
This is more calm surrender.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:12.806
Yeah.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:16.009
Andre, do it again.

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:17.510
Tsch!

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:18.244
There you go.

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:19.846
That's the one.

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:22.215
So whatever you did and whatever
that is, that's the intensity.

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:24.217
So you don't have to,
like, do it three times.

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:25.618
JENNIFER: This is huge
for her because she

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:26.152
normally would've been--

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:27.587
CESAR: Yeah.

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:29.556
And this is her true nature,
her happy go-lucky self

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:30.256
that we all love.

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:31.991
There you go.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:34.627
This is more calm surrender.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:37.430
Bella and Jennifer are
doing great so far.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.899
So now I'm going to push
their limits a little

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:42.802
and see how they react when
confronted with another dog.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:43.703
Andre!

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.071
ANDRE: Yes, sir.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:47.307
CESAR: I have my son Andre move
in slowly with the other dog

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:49.609
to prevent Bella from
feeling threatened.

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:53.079
I want to see how Bella
chooses to react to a dog

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:54.714
entering her space calmly.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.950
Tsch!

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:59.853
Tsch!

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:03.356
[dogs whining, panting]

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.628
So now we have two
calm surrender.

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:09.262
Can you see it?

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:10.396
JENNIFER: Mm-hmm.

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:11.931
So that's why
it's so important

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:15.001
to assess and evaluate how
they feel, not what they did,

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:16.703
what they're doing right now.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.137
JENNIFER: Right.

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:19.806
Yawning is good.

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:21.341
A yawn equals relaxation.

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:22.842
It means calm surrender.

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:26.012
Bella has a troubled past,
but you can see that that's

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:28.014
not going to define her future.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.616
When I do walk
her, I usually put

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.150
the weighted vest
and her goggles

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.185
on just to help decrease.

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:32.752
I want to see the whole thing.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:34.153
OK.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.889
I'm so proud of all the
work Jennifer has put in.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:39.592
She's even using tools like
weighted vest to burn energy.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:40.693
She looks-- oh my!

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:41.728
They have pink?

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:42.662
JENNIFER: Yeah!

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:43.630
CESAR: Oh, my lord!

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:44.430
JENNIFER: [chuckles]

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:45.899
CESAR: I love it even more!

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.166
JENNIFER: Yeah.

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:49.469
When we put it on her,
she's much calmer.

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:52.505
CESAR: And goggles, they'll
work like blinders on a horse.

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:56.543
Together, it's all about
controlling Bella's excitement.

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:57.777
We're ready.

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.679
NARRATOR: Showing great
success remaining calm when

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:02.248
faced with old
triggers, Cesar takes

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:05.885
this once red-zone pit bull
for a final neighborhood walk.

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:07.387
Yeah.

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:09.222
When I first met Jennifer,
she was getting dragged down

00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:12.058
the streets by a dog
ready to fight anyone

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:13.326
that stepped in their path.

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:15.695
These dogs never got
exercise because it

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:17.530
wasn't safe to walk them.

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:20.066
So now I want to see
how Jennifer handles

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:22.101
a walk with all the
tools and knowledge

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:24.404
she's gained throughout
Bella's rehabilitation.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.039
Don't forget distance also.

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:26.940
Look, turn this way.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:28.074
There you go.

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.709
Distance is respect.

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:31.945
We were so concerned
that we would have to find

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.346
Bella a new place to live.

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:35.615
Then, working with Cesar,
learning all the tools,

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:37.283
and see that she's
happy go-lucky,

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:40.119
and she's not really responding
as much to other dogs,

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:41.220
it made me feel better.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:42.789
And giving her a second chance--

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.290
it's all thanks to Cesar.

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:46.993
[inhales deeply]
Much better, right?

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:47.961
Yeah, this was great.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:48.595
Yeah, this is it.

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:49.963
Uh-huh.

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.864
Normally, she would have already
been barking by now at them.

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:54.801
CESAR: She's actually in a
super happy, go-lucky feeling

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.202
right now, so enjoy this point.

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:57.070
Just like you--

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:57.837
Yeah, this is good.

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.072
Yeah, exactly.

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:00.239
So let's focus on
those little moments

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:01.441
where it's just awesome.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:02.976
ANDRE: Seeing the
progress has actually

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.445
fueled my fire to keep on
progressing with all the dogs.

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:07.347
Cesar, I just
wanted to thank you.

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:10.416
And there's nothing I could
say that would repay what

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:11.818
you've done for our family.

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:13.853
It was awesome to be a
first responder for once.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.788
[laughs] Well,
you definitely were.

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:16.889
Appreciate you very much.

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:17.957
You did amazing.

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:21.527
[music playing]

